{"tool_name":"coot","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"coot","home":"http://www2.mrc-lmb.cam.ac.uk/personal/pemsley/coot/","summary":"(Crystallographic Object)-Oriented Toolkit.","addition_date":"2015-03-26T22:59:14Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T20:08:21.627874Z","tool_type":["Desktop application"],"version":["0.9"],"collections":["CCP4"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:coot","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"ccisb@stfc.ac.uk","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"name":"Instruct","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://www2.mrc-lmb.cam.ac.uk/personal/pemsley/coot/"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["mwinn","sergitobara"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Protein structure","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1460"}}],"note":"For macromolecular model building, model completion and validation, particularly suitable for protein modelling using X-ray data. Coot displays maps and models and allows model manipulations such as idealization, real space refinement, manual rotation/translation, rigid-body fitting, ligand search, solvation, mutations, rotamers, Ramachandran plots, skeletonization, non-crystallographic symmetry and more.For Windows version, see WinCoot.","operation":[{"term":"Structure visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0570"}]}],"name":"Coot","operating_system":["Linux","Mac"],"owner":"Instruct","publication":[{"doi":"10.1107/s0907444910007493","metadata":{"abstract":"Coot is a molecular-graphics application for model building and validation of biological macromolecules. The program displays electron-density maps and atomic models and allows model manipulations such as idealization, real-space refinement, manual rotation/translation, rigid-body fitting, ligand search, solvation, mutations, rotamers and Ramachandran idealization. Furthermore, tools are provided for model validation as well as interfaces to external programs for refinement, validation and graphics. The software is designed to be easy to learn for novice users, which is achieved by ensuring that tools for common tasks are discoverable through familiar user-interface elements (menus and toolbars) or by intuitive behaviour (mouse controls). Recent developments have focused on providing tools for expert users, with customisable key bindings, extensions and an extensive scripting interface. The software is under rapid development, but has already achieved very widespread use within the crystallographic community. The current state of the software is presented, with a description of the facilities available and of some of the underlying methods employed.","authors":[{"name":"Cowtan K."},{"name":"Emsley P."},{"name":"Lohkamp B."},{"name":"Scott W.G."}],"citationCount":20670,"date":"2010-04-19T00:00:00Z","journal":"Acta Crystallographica Section D: Biological Crystallography","title":"Features and development of Coot"},"pmcid":"PMC2852313","pmid":"20383002","type":["Primary"]},{"doi":"10.1107/s0907444904019158","metadata":{"abstract":"CCP4mg is a project that aims to provide a general-purpose tool for structural biologists, providing tools for X-ray structure solution, structure comparison and analysis, and publication-quality graphics. The map-fitting tools are available as a stand-alone package, distributed as 'Coot'. \u00a9 2004 International Union of Crystallography - all rights reserved.","authors":[{"name":"Cowtan K."},{"name":"Emsley P."}],"citationCount":25709,"date":"2004-12-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Acta Crystallographica Section D: Biological Crystallography","title":"Coot: Model-building tools for molecular graphics"},"pmid":"15572765","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Structural biology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_1317"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"Coot","home":"https://bio.tools/coot","version":"0.9","summary":"(Crystallographic Object)-Oriented Toolkit.